<script language="javascript" src="../../_dwr/interface/NewsvoteDWR.js"></script><script language="javascript" src="../../_dwr/engine.js"></script><script language="javascript" src="/system/resource/js/news/newscontent.js"></script><LINK href="/system/resource/js/photoswipe/3.0.5.1/photoswipe.css" type="text/css" rel="stylesheet"><script language="javascript" src="/system/resource/js/photoswipe/3.0.5.1/pw.js"></script><link rel="stylesheet" Content-type="text/css" href="/system/resource/style/component/news/content/format2.css"><script language="javascript" src="/system/resource/js/ajax.js"></script><form name="_newscontent_fromname">
<div class="show-news show-study">
<div class="show-news01">
    <h5 align="center" style="font-weight:bold;">XDU Shen Jai Confucius Institute in Malaysia Carries Out Chinese Language Teaching and Cultural Exchange Activities</h5>
	<p><i>Time:&nbsp;May 8, 2026</i></p></div>
	<div id="vsb_content_2" style="font-size: 18px;color: #333333;line-height: 30px;text-align: justify;"><div class="v_news_content">
<p class="vsbcontent_img"></p><p>Recently, XDU Shen Jai Confucius Institute in Malaysia held cultural exchange activities at several local schools and universities. Featuring Chinese language courses, intangible cultural heritage handcrafts and cultural comparisons, the sessions offered immersive Chinese cultural experiences.</p><p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/__local/8/83/EF/C768FDDFC74B770A61F1E04733E_15064125_2D931.jpeg" vsbhref="vurl" vurl="/_vsl/883EFC768FDDFC74B770A61F1E04733E/15064125/2D931" vheight=" 310.75pt" vwidth=" 414.6pt" orisrc="/__local/A/B8/47/5399D9792AD0693F2DC261EA8FF_E77A4545_2D9A8.jpeg" class="img_vsb_content" style="text-align: center; text-indent: 0px; white-space: normal; width: 414.6pt; height: 310.75pt;"></p><p class="vsbcontent_img"><img src="/__local/9/D5/40/A0DC9FFA70A0FF6E7CC47932651_F2356444_2C128.jpeg" vsbhref="vurl" vurl="/_vsl/9D540A0DC9FFA70A0FF6E7CC47932651/F2356444/2C128" vheight=" 279.65pt" vwidth=" 373.05pt" orisrc="/__local/8/78/0A/76AE9E87098E67BF7DF2809BAB4_4B2FA674_2C149.jpeg" class="img_vsb_content" style="width: 373.05pt;height: 279.65pt"></p><p>During these events, local teachers and students participated in paper quilling art and bamboo culture workshops. The Confucius Institute demonstrated practical craft skills, helping participants gain deeper insights into traditional Chinese culture.</p><p class="vsbcontent_end">The Institute will continue to strengthen China-Malaysia cultural exchanges and promote mutual understanding and friendship between the two countries.</p><p class="vsbcontent_img"><img src="/__local/4/AD/B6/5E170BE52F65A14BA27636AE113_068B0115_14EA1.jpeg" vsbhref="vurl" vurl="/_vsl/4ADB65E170BE52F65A14BA27636AE113/068B0115/14EA1" vheight=" 321.15pt" vwidth=" 241.8pt" orisrc="/__local/8/D2/0C/42CA70495D7072C9BEFDB88E001_7A2C5C3A_13EA3.jpeg" class="img_vsb_content" style="width: 241.8pt;height: 321.15pt"></p>
</div></div><div id="div_vote_id"></div>
